<details>
<summary>How Much Does Auto Repair Cost vs. Buying New?</summary>
<div>Every repair estimate at Duft Auto comes in writing before work begins, so the cost of fixing a vehicle is clear before any decision gets made. A repair addressing a single failed component — a brake job, an alternator, a diagnostic-flagged sensor — costs a fraction of a vehicle payment and often restores full function for years of continued use. Duft Auto walks through the repair-versus-replace tradeoff directly with the customer before any parts get ordered, not after the invoice arrives. Vehicles with isolated mechanical issues rarely justify replacement over repair.</div>
</details>
<details>
<summary>How Do I Know My Vehicle Needs Service?</summary>
<ul>
<li>Grinding, squealing, or soft brakes</li>
<li>Check engine or dashboard warning light</li>
<li>Vibration or pulling at highway speed</li>
<li>Rough idle, stalling, or hard starts</li>
<li>Visible fluid leaks under the vehicle</li>
</ul>
</details>
<details>
<summary>What Does the Repair Process Involve at Duft Auto?</summary>
<div>A visit starts with a scheduled appointment — no walk-in wait, no guessing when a bay opens up. Auggie runs a diagnostic scan paired with a physical inspection to confirm the actual cause of the issue, not just the code the vehicle's computer throws. Findings get explained in plain language, with a written estimate covering parts and labor before any work starts. Same-day turnaround applies to most routine jobs — oil changes, brake service, and tire installation — while larger diagnostic or engine repairs get a realistic timeline up front.</div>
</details>
<details>
